    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (**BUILD SUCCESS**).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification defined membership level 4 as requiring tenure of more than 365 days, but the code never actually implemented it \u2014 `MembershipLevel.of` hard-capped at 3 with a comment saying \"level 4 is reserved for tenure.\" I made level 4 reachable via tenure while ensuring new owners stay at level 3.\n\n**`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 the email + `namesakeCount` factors are still capped at 3, then a tenure factor adds +1 (reaching 4) only when tenure exceeds 365 days:\n- `tenureDays(owner)` = days from `registrationDate` to today, floored at 0 (and 0 when the date is absent).\n- A newly created owner has `registrationDate` = today \u2192 tenure 0 \u2192 no bump \u2192 stays at level 3. The maxed pre-tenure case (email present, `namesakeCount` 0) lands at exactly 3, not 4.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipLevel` schema (`maximum: 3` \u2192 `4`) and its description to match the new rule, keeping the API contract consistent.\n\nThe `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test (new owner with email \u2192 expects level 3) passes, and the full suite is green.",
